\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Per-problem sync wall-time (x) vs async wall-time (y), one dot per problem. Dots below the diagonal are problems on which async is faster than sync. The C++ cloud sits visibly below the diagonal at every cost level; the Rust cloud crowds the diagonal at the cheap end (where the verifier is fast and sync is already adequate) but still skews under it.}}{14}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:speedup-scatter}{{7}{14}{Per-problem sync wall-time (x) vs async wall-time (y), one dot per problem. Dots below the diagonal are problems on which async is faster than sync. The C++ cloud sits visibly below the diagonal at every cost level; the Rust cloud crowds the diagonal at the cheap end (where the verifier is fast and sync is already adequate) but still skews under it}{figure.7}{}}
