\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Distribution of rollback counts per problem, faceted by language $\times $ scheduling. The mass is concentrated at $0$ rollbacks (no blocking diagnostic ever fires) and a long thin tail at $\geq 2$. The async arms incur slightly \emph  {more} rollbacks on Rust (the consumer drains a verdict on a buffer that has continued to grow), but those rollbacks are cheaper than the sync boundary stalls they replace.}}{15}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rollback-dist}{{8}{15}{Distribution of rollback counts per problem, faceted by language $\times $ scheduling. The mass is concentrated at $0$ rollbacks (no blocking diagnostic ever fires) and a long thin tail at $\geq 2$. The async arms incur slightly \emph {more} rollbacks on Rust (the consumer drains a verdict on a buffer that has continued to grow), but those rollbacks are cheaper than the sync boundary stalls they replace}{figure.8}{}}
